[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Character Movement Component Customization and Prediction in Unreal Engine"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Unreal Engine uses a robust network prediction model inside the Character Movement Component (CMC) to handle client-side prediction and server reconciliation. When designing custom movement modes or altering existing physics, understanding how to extend this prediction loop is essential for preventing stutter and rubberbanding."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Extending the Character Movement Component"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"To add custom movement logic, you must create a subclass of UCharacterMovementComponent. This allows you to override core functions like UpdateAnimatedMove, PhysCustom, and PerformClientMovement."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"UCLASS()
class UMyCustomMovementComponent : public UCharacterMovementComponent
{
    GENERATED_BODY()
public:
    virtual void PhysCustom(float deltaTime, int32 iterations) override;
};"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"Implementing Custom Movement Modes"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"The CMC natively supports a custom movement mode enumeration (MOVE_Custom). You can use this state to implement unique mechanics like sliding, wall-running, or grappling."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Set the movement mode to MOVE_Custom using SetMovementMode(MOVE_Custom, CustomSubMode)."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Handle the physics calculation inside PhysCustom by checking your custom sub-mode."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Ensure all velocity and position updates respect the passed delta time for deterministic simulation."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Network Prediction and Saved Moves"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"For your custom movement to function correctly in multiplayer, you must encapsulate client inputs inside a custom FSavedMove_Character struct and handle network data serialization via FNetworkPredictionData_Client_Character."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"class FSavedMove_MyCustom : public FSavedMove_Character
{
public:
    typedef FSavedMove_Character Super;

    uint8 bCustomPayload : 1;

    virtual void Clear() override;
    virtual uint8 GetCompressedFlags() const override;
    virtual void SetMoveFor(ACharacter* C, float InDeltaTime, FVector const& NewAccel, FNetworkPredictionData_Client_Character& ClientData) override;
};"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for Smooth Replication"},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always validate inputs on the server to prevent cheating."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Keep custom state flags tightly packed within compressed flags to minimize bandwidth usage."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Test your movement implementation under simulated high latency and packet loss conditions using network emulation settings."}]
